From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] kmsdrm: SDL_KMSDRM_DEFAULT_CURSOR=0 creates no default cursor (RelicOS)

KMSDRM_InitMouse creates the default arrow cursor unconditionally, and a
program that never calls SDL_ShowCursor(SDL_DISABLE) shows it on the DRM
cursor plane, in a corner, for as long as it runs -- PortMaster's interface
on the R36S (M26): there is no pointing device on this handheld, only a
gamepad. The ES and RetroArch hide it themselves; a third-party program
cannot be asked to. This hint (read from the environment, like every SDL
hint) skips the default cursor; a cursor the program creates and sets is
untouched, so a port with a mouse cursor of its own keeps it. Default on:
nothing changes unless the launcher asks.
---
diff -ruN a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmvideo.h"
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmmouse.h"
+#include "SDL_hints.h"
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmdyn.h"
 
 #include "../../events/SDL_mouse_c.h"
@@ -408,9 +409,15 @@
     mouse->WarpMouseGlobal = KMSDRM_WarpMouseGlobal;
 
     /* Only create the default cursor for this display if we haven't done so before,
-       we don't want several cursors to be created for the same display. */
+       we don't want several cursors to be created for the same display.
+       RelicOS: SDL_KMSDRM_DEFAULT_CURSOR=0 (hint or environment) creates none:
+       on a handheld with no pointing device the arrow only ever sits in a
+       corner of any program that does not hide it. A cursor the program sets
+       itself (SDL_CreateCursor + SDL_SetCursor) still shows. */
     if (!dispdata->default_cursor_init) {
-        SDL_SetDefaultCursor(KMSDRM_CreateDefaultCursor());
+        if (SDL_GetHintBoolean("SDL_KMSDRM_DEFAULT_CURSOR", SDL_TRUE)) {
+            SDL_SetDefaultCursor(KMSDRM_CreateDefaultCursor());
+        }
         dispdata->default_cursor_init = SDL_TRUE;
     }
 }
